.TH GET-PREREQS.SH 1 "2026-04-25" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
get-prereqs.sh \- install required tools for GitMirror scripts on Ubuntu/Debian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash get-prereqs.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get-prereqs.sh
checks for
.B curl
and
.B jq
and installs any missing package using
.B apt-get
with
.B sudo
.
.PP
The script is intended for Ubuntu/Debian systems and runs:
.IP "1."
.B sudo apt-get update
.IP "2."
.B sudo apt-get install -y curl
or
.B jq
as needed.
.PP
When complete, it prints detected versions of both tools.
.SH OPTIONS
This command has no options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success. Exits non-zero if package installation fails or if commands cannot be executed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install prerequisites for other GitMirror scripts:
.PP
.B bash get-prereqs.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1)
